{"url": "https://www.utrgv.edu/admissions/graduate/resources/grad-application-fee/index.htm", "final_url": "https://www.utrgv.edu/admissions/graduate/resources/grad-application-fee/index.htm", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-11-14", "text": "Graduate Application Fee Information | UTRGV\nSkip to main content\nUTRGV Admissions | #1 Ranked University in Texas | Explore Programs & Deadlines\nFreshman\nTransfer\nInternational\nReturning\nGraduate\nNon-Degree\nFor Families\nApply Now\nVisit Campus\nExplore Programs\nRequest Info\nCheck Status\nContact Us\nDIRECTORY\nMAPS\nMYUTRGV\nNEWS\nGIVE\nThe University of Texas\nRio Grande Valley\nDIRECTORY\nMAPS\nMYUTRGV\nNews\nGIVE\nOpen Search Menu\nMenu\nSearch\nClear\nSearch\nAdmissions\nFreshman\nTransfer\nInternational\nReturning\nGraduate\nNon-Degree\nFor Families\nApply Now\nVisit Campus\nExplore Programs\nRequest Info\nCheck Status\nContact Us\nGraduate Admissions\nGraduate Application Fee Information\nHome\nGraduate Admissions\nApplication Resources\nGraduate Application Fee Information\nApplication Resources Menu\nMenu\nApplication Resources Menu\nConditional Admission\nGRE & GMAT Entrance Exams\nEnglish Proficiency Exam\nForeign Credential Evaluation\nGraduate Application Fee Information\nGraduate Program Coordinator\nSchedule an Appointment with a Recruiter\nViewbooks\nAt The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV), we are proud to make graduate education accessible and affordable. Most of our graduate programs currently do not require an application fee. However, application fees are non-refundable for programs that do require them.\nBelow is a list of the programs with an application fee:\nCommunication Sciences and Disorders (COMD)\nFamily Nurse Practitioner (Post Master's Certificate)\nOccupational Therapy (OTD)\nPhysician Assistant Studies (MPAS)\nPhysical Therapy (DPT)\nPsychiatric/Mental Health Nurse Practitioner Certificate Program\nApplication Fee Details:\nDomestic Applicants: $50.00\nInternational Applicants: $100.00\nGraduate Admissions\nLocations\nBrownsville Campus:\nSabal Hall 1.202\nEdinburg Campus:\nMarialice Shary Shivers (MASS) Bldg. 1.158\nContact Information\nEmail: gradrecruitment@utrgv.edu\nPhone: 1-833-887-4842\nText: 956-996-8095\nWhatsApp: 956-996-8035\nFind us on Social Media\nLIKE. FOLLOW. SUBSCRIBE. ADD.\nMy Texas Future is a state-supported resource that helps Texans explore careers, find college programs, and access financial aid options to start, return to, or advance their education.\nClery Act\nThe Annual Security and Fire Safety Report includes information on safety and security policies, including crime and fire statistics for the previous three years.\nThe report is available on the University Police website. A hard copy of the report is available at the University Police Departments located on 501 N. Sugar Rd. (Edinburg), 2671 FJRM Ave. (Brownsville), 2102 Treasure Hills Blvd. (Harlingen), or 1937 East Bustamante Street (Laredo), also by contacting University Police at 956-882-7777.\nCARES, CRRSAA and ARP Reporting\nSite Policies\nRequired Links\nAccreditation Statement\nFraud Reporting\nSenate Bill 18\nClery Act Reports\nWeb Accessibility\nMental Health Resources\nSexual Misconduct Policy\nReporting Sexual Misconduct\nContact UTRGV\n1-844-ATUTRGV\nAcademics\nAdmissions\nCost and Financial Aid\nStudent Life\nSearch Programs\nFirst-Year Students\nTransfer\nInternational Students\nGraduate Students\nCurrent Students\nFaculty Resources\nStaff Resources\nUTRGV Careers\nVisit Campus\nDirectory\nThe University of Texas Rio Grande Valley", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.utrgv.edu/admissions/graduate/resources/grad-application-fee/index.htm#maincontent"], ["UTRGV Admissions | #1 Ranked University in Texas | Explore Programs & Deadlines", "https://www.utrgv.edu/admissions/index.htm"], ["Freshman", "https://www.utrgv.edu/admissions/freshman/index.htm"], ["Transfer", "https://www.utrgv.edu/admissions/transfer/inde